---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="Prime AI Company — open-model training on customer datasets.">
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 md:py-24">
    <p class="section-label">About</p>
    <h1 class="heading-display mt-2 text-3xl md:text-4xl">{site.name}</h1>
    <p class="copy-bridge mt-4">Training agency — open LLMs and diffusion on your data.</p>
    <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted">
      Clients bring domain data; we bring dataset engineering, GPU training, evaluation, and deployment documentation.
    </p>
    <p class="p-instrument mt-4 text-[13px]">
      No customer A data in customer B models. Weights and adapters belong to you under contract.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-12 text-xl font-semibold">Principles</h2>
    <ul class="mt-4 space-y-4 text-muted">
      <li>
        <strong class="text-text">Your weights, your contract.</strong> Fine-tuned artifacts are delivered to you per statement of work. We do not train customer A’s data into customer B’s models.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong class="text-text">Open stacks.</strong> We prefer inspectable, self-hostable models over perpetual API rent when requirements allow.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong class="text-text">Safety by default.</strong> License review, consent for likeness training, and eval gates are part of standard delivery—not add-on surprises.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong class="text-text">Infrastructure you trust.</strong> Training runs on enterprise clouds with VPC options for regulated workloads.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p class="copy-caption mt-12">
      New projects: <a href={`mailto:${site.emails.sales}`} class="text-instrument hover:opacity-90">{site.emails.sales}</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
